Z||000005||Monkeyman||01-28-2000||09:17 PM||||Indiana is based on the age and original price of the vehicle.  Anything older than 10 years is a flat $28.75.  Unless you get personalized plates.  That adds another $45/year, but it's worth it.  Ohio is a flat fee.  (At least in the county where my wifes car is registered)  About $45 if I remember correctly.  Doesn't matter what year or how much it cost.  (Thank God!)||||reg||1
Z||000006||fiero56||01-28-2000||09:22 PM||||I just dug up the receipt for tags on my '88 Fiero in Ohio. I paid 22.53 for tags. I don't know if it varies by county but mine is registered in Mongomery.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Standard||01-29-2000||12:16 AM||||I paid 38.75 for my 84 SC here in Minnesota.  don't know how they set prices, tho.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Monkeyman||01-29-2000||09:53 AM||||My wifes car was 1st registered in Butler Co., now in Clearfield (maybe Clearwater or something like that) Co.  One of the reasons she chose to keep the registration in Ohio is/was because of the $$.  Indiana would have cost us more like $350 this year.  (She paid too much for her car.)||||reg||1
